solution:
The factors have the same positive base, so multiplying them adds their exponents:
\[
256^{0.16}\cdot256^{0.09}
=256^{0.16+0.09}
=256^{0.25}
=256^{1/4}.
\]
The exponent \(1/4\) means the positive fourth root. Since \(4^4=256\), the value is \(4\), choice A.

